insert into public.drug_info (drug_id, rxcui, matched_name, uses, how_to_take, warnings, side_effects, interactions, source_url, fetched_at) values ($t$134aa864-bfc9-4cf7-a372-937c46ec78f3$t$, $t$3992$t$, $t$epinephrine$t$, $t$Epinephrine is a non-selective alpha and beta adrenergic agonist indicated to increase mean arterial blood pressure in adult patients with hypotension associated with septic shock. 1.1 Hypotension associated with Septic Shock Epinephrine Injection USP, 1 mg/10 mL (0.1 mg/mL) is indicated to increase mean arterial blood pressure in adult patients with hypotension associated with septic shock.$t$, $t$2 DOSAGE AND ADMINISTRATION • Hypotension associated with septic shock : o Dilute epinephrine in dextrose solution prior to infusion. o Infuse epinephrine into a large vein. o Titrate 0.05 mcg/kg/min to 2 mcg/kg/min to achieve desired blood pressure. o Wean gradually. 2.1 General Considerations Inspect visually for particulate matter and discoloration prior to administration, whenever solution and container permit. Do not use if the solution is colored or cloudy, or if it contains particulate matter. …$t$, $t$5 WARNINGS AND PRECAUTIONS • Monitor blood pressure frequently. • Increases cardiac output and causes peripheral vasoconstriction. • May induce cardiac arrhythmias and myocardial ischemia. • Avoid extravasation into tissues, which can cause local necrosis. • Constricts renal blood vessels which may result in oliguria or renal impairment. • Sulfite Warning. …$t$, $t$6 ADVERSE REACTIONS • Hypertension • Pulmonary Edema • Cardiac Arrhythmias and Ischemia • Extravassation and Tissue Necrosis with Intravenous Infusion • Renal Impairment • Allergic Reactions associated with Sulfite The following adverse reactions associated with the infusion of epinephrine were identified in the literature. …$t$, $t$Drugs that counter the pressor effects of epinephrine include alpha blockers, vasodilators such as nitrates, diuretics, antihypertensives, and ergot alkaloids. ( 7 .1) Drugs that potentiate the effects of epinephrine include sympathomimetics, beta blockers, tricyclic antidepressants, MAO inhibitors, COMT inhibitors, clonidine, doxapram, oxytocin, levothyroxine sodium, and certain antihistamines. …$t$, $t$https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/lookup.cfm?setid=0172280c-f7d6-4613-9dbd-f94d3ae5825a$t$, now())
